---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Layout
  title="Streamlining HR Data with Google BigQuery | Case Study"
  description="Transforming disconnected HR systems into a unified engine for strategic decision-making using automated Google BigQuery pipelines."
>
  <div class="py-16 sm:py-24 lg:py-32">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      
      <!-- BREADCRUMB -->
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-slate-500 mb-8">
        <a href={`${base}/projects`} class="hover:text-emerald-700 transition-colors">Case Studies</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-slate-800 font-medium">BigQuery Architecture</span>
      </nav>

      <!-- TITLE HEADER -->
      <div class="max-w-4xl mb-16 sm:mb-20">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-50 border border-emerald-200/80 px-4 py-1.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-emerald-800 shadow-sm mb-6">
          <span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
          Data Engineering Blueprint
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-6xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-950 font-sans leading-tight">
          Streamlining HR Data: From Chaos to Clarity with Google BigQuery
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 text-xl sm:text-2xl text-slate-600 font-normal leading-relaxed">
          Transforming disconnected HR systems into a unified engine for strategic decision-making.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- THE PROBLEM HERO CARD -->
      <div class="rounded-3xl border border-white/70 bg-white/60 p-8 sm:p-12 backdrop-blur-2xl shadow-[0_12px_40px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04),inset_0_1px_1px_rgba(255,255,255,0.95)] mb-16 sm:mb-24">
        <div class="text-xs font-extrabold uppercase tracking-widest text-emerald-700 font-mono mb-3">
          The Problem
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-950 font-sans tracking-tight mb-4">
          The High Cost of Disconnected HR Data
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            For many HR Directors and business leaders, answering a simple question like <em class="text-slate-800 font-medium">"What is our turnover rate correlated with recent compensation changes?"</em> is an agonizing, multi-day process.
          </p>
          <p>
            Why? Because HR data is inherently messy and scattered. Your recruitment data lives in an Applicant Tracking System (ATS), compensation sits in Payroll, employee sentiment is trapped in a survey platform, and historical performance reviews are buried in endless Excel spreadsheets.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- WHERE THE WORK GETS STUCK -->
      <section class="mb-20 sm:mb-28">
        <div class="text-xs font-extrabold uppercase tracking-widest text-emerald-700 font-mono mb-3">
          Bottlenecks
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-950 font-sans tracking-tight mb-8">
          Where the work gets stuck
        </h2>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
          <div class="rounded-3xl border border-white/70 bg-white/55 p-8 backdrop-blur-2xl shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgba(0,0,0,0.03),inset_0_1px_1px_rgba(255,255,255,0.9)]">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950 font-sans">Wasted Time</h3>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              Your HR team spends hours every week manually exporting CSVs, running complex VLOOKUPs, and cleaning data instead of actually analyzing it.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-3xl border border-white/70 bg-white/55 p-8 backdrop-blur-2xl shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgba(0,0,0,0.03),inset_0_1px_1px_rgba(255,255,255,0.9)]">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950 font-sans">Reactive Blind Spots</h3>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              By the time a report is compiled, the data is already stale, making it impossible to proactively address flight risks or burnout.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-3xl border border-white/70 bg-white/55 p-8 backdrop-blur-2xl shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgba(0,0,0,0.03),inset_0_1px_1px_rgba(255,255,255,0.9)]">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950 font-sans">Data Trust Issues</h3>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              When leadership gets conflicting numbers because "my spreadsheet hasn't been updated yet," trust in HR metrics erodes.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SECTION 01: THE ARCHITECTURE -->
      <section class="mb-20 sm:mb-28">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center h-12 w-12 rounded-2xl bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-700 font-mono text-xl font-extrabold shadow-sm">
            01
          </span>
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-950 font-sans tracking-tight">
              The Architecture: Unifying Your People Data
            </h2>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl">
          To solve this, we don't need to replace your existing HR software. Instead, we build an automated bridge. Below is the architecture strategy I use to pull data out of isolated silos and organize it into a single, highly secure data warehouse.
        </p>

        <!-- ZERO-JS RESPONSIVE FLOW DIAGRAM -->
        <div class="rounded-3xl border border-white/80 bg-white/70 p-8 sm:p-12 backdrop-blur-2xl shadow-[0_12px_40px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04),inset_0_1px_1px_rgba(255,255,255,0.95)]">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6 items-center">
            
            <!-- Stage 1: Isolated Sources -->
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 font-mono text-center lg:text-left mb-2">Data Sources</div>
              <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-200/80 p-4 shadow-sm text-center lg:text-left">
                <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500">Applicant Tracking</div>
                <div class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">Lever / Greenhouse</div>
              </div>
              <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-200/80 p-4 shadow-sm text-center lg:text-left">
                <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500">Payroll & HRIS</div>
                <div class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">ADP / Gusto / Workday</div>
              </div>
              <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-200/80 p-4 shadow-sm text-center lg:text-left">
                <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500">Employee Surveys</div>
                <div class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">CultureAmp / Qualtrics</div>
              </div>
              <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-200/80 p-4 shadow-sm text-center lg:text-left">
                <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500">Ad-hoc Records</div>
                <div class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">Excel / Google Sheets</div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Arrow 1 -->
            <div class="flex justify-center text-emerald-500">
              <svg class="h-8 w-8 hidden lg:block" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.5" d="M14 5l7 7m0 0l-7 7m7-7H3"/>
              </svg>
              <svg class="h-8 w-8 lg:hidden" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.5" d="M19 14l-7 7m0 0l-7-7m7 7V3"/>
              </svg>
            </div>

            <!-- Stage 2: Automated Pipeline & Warehouse -->
            <div class="space-y-4">
              <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-700 font-mono text-center lg:text-left mb-2">Automated Core</div>
              <div class="rounded-2xl bg-emerald-50 border border-emerald-300 p-5 shadow-sm text-center lg:text-left">
                <div class="text-xs font-extrabold uppercase tracking-widest text-emerald-800 font-mono">Automated ETL</div>
                <div class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-950 mt-1">Extraction & Cleaning Pipeline</div>
                <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-2">Deduplicates, validates schema, and normalizes employee IDs.</p>
              </div>

              <div class="rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-900 to-slate-950 text-white p-5 shadow-xl text-center lg:text-left border border-white/20">
                <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-emerald-400 font-mono">Central Warehouse</div>
                <div class="text-base font-extrabold mt-1">Google BigQuery</div>
                <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 mt-2">Serverless, masked sensitive fields, encrypted at rest.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Stage 3: Executive BI Dashboard -->
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-cyan-700 font-mono text-center lg:text-left mb-2">Leadership View</div>
              <div class="rounded-2xl bg-cyan-50/80 border border-cyan-300 p-6 shadow-sm text-center lg:text-left">
                <div class="text-xs font-extrabold uppercase tracking-widest text-cyan-800 font-mono">Real-Time BI Dashboard</div>
                <div class="text-base font-bold text-slate-950 mt-1">Power BI / Looker Studio</div>
                <ul class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-3 space-y-1 text-left list-disc list-inside">
                  <li>Real-time voluntary turnover rates</li>
                  <li>Headcount by department & seniority</li>
                  <li>Flight-risk early warnings</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SECTION 02: WHY GOOGLE BIGQUERY -->
      <section class="mb-20 sm:mb-28">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center h-12 w-12 rounded-2xl bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-700 font-mono text-xl font-extrabold shadow-sm">
            02
          </span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-950 font-sans tracking-tight">
            The Solution Strategy: Why Google BigQuery?
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl">
          For Small to Medium-Sized Businesses (SMBs), building a data warehouse might sound like an expensive, enterprise-only endeavor. But <strong class="text-slate-950 font-bold">Google BigQuery</strong> is cheap and scalable, making it the absolute best choice for growing HR teams:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
          <div class="rounded-3xl border border-white/70 bg-white/55 p-8 backdrop-blur-2xl shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgba(0,0,0,0.03),inset_0_1px_1px_rgba(255,255,255,0.9)]">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950 font-sans">Cost-Effective (Pay-As-You-Go)</h3>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              You don't need to buy massive servers. BigQuery is "serverless," meaning you only pay for the exact queries you run. For most SMB HR datasets, the storage and processing costs are mere pennies a month.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-3xl border border-white/70 bg-white/55 p-8 backdrop-blur-2xl shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgba(0,0,0,0.03),inset_0_1px_1px_rgba(255,255,255,0.9)]">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950 font-sans">Enterprise-Grade Security</h3>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              HR data is highly sensitive. BigQuery is backed by Google’s world-class security infrastructure, allowing us to set strict access controls. We can easily mask sensitive fields (like salaries or social security numbers) so only authorized leadership can view them.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-3xl border border-white/70 bg-white/55 p-8 backdrop-blur-2xl shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgba(0,0,0,0.03),inset_0_1px_1px_rgba(255,255,255,0.9)]">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950 font-sans">Zero-Maintenance Scalability</h3>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              Whether your company has 50 employees or 5,000, BigQuery handles the load effortlessly. As your business grows, your data architecture doesn't have to change.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-3xl border border-white/70 bg-white/55 p-8 backdrop-blur-2xl shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgba(0,0,0,0.03),inset_0_1px_1px_rgba(255,255,255,0.9)]">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950 font-sans">Seamless Integration</h3>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              It connects natively to powerful Business Intelligence tools, turning raw code into beautiful, interactive dashboards that anyone on the executive team can understand.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SECTION 03: BUSINESS IMPACT & ROI -->
      <section class="mb-20 sm:mb-28">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center h-12 w-12 rounded-2xl bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-700 font-mono text-xl font-extrabold shadow-sm">
            03
          </span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-950 font-sans tracking-tight">
            The Business Impact
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl">
          By centralizing your HR data into BigQuery and layering a visual dashboard on top, we shift the HR function from a tactical cost center to a strategic business partner.
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
          <div class="rounded-3xl border border-white/70 bg-white/55 p-8 backdrop-blur-2xl shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgba(0,0,0,0.03),inset_0_1px_1px_rgba(255,255,255,0.9)]">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950 font-sans">Saved Time</h3>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              Complete elimination of manual data entry and spreadsheet consolidation. Reports that used to take days now refresh automatically in seconds.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-3xl border border-white/70 bg-white/55 p-8 backdrop-blur-2xl shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgba(0,0,0,0.03),inset_0_1px_1px_rgba(255,255,255,0.9)]">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950 font-sans">A Single Source of Truth</h3>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              End the meeting-room debates over whose numbers are correct. Everyone works from the same live, validated dataset.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-3xl border border-white/70 bg-white/55 p-8 backdrop-blur-2xl shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgba(0,0,0,0.03),inset_0_1px_1px_rgba(255,255,255,0.9)]">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950 font-sans">Predictive Turnover Modeling</h3>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              Move from asking <em>"Who left last quarter?"</em> to <em>"Who is showing signs of leaving next quarter?"</em> by correlating engagement scores with compensation gaps.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-3xl border border-white/70 bg-white/55 p-8 backdrop-blur-2xl shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgba(0,0,0,0.03),inset_0_1px_1px_rgba(255,255,255,0.9)]">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950 font-sans">Strategic Agility</h3>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
              Instantly view real-time metrics on headcount pacing, diversity initiatives, and compensation equity at the click of a button.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- BACK TO PROJECTS & CTA -->
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-6 rounded-3xl border border-white/70 bg-white/60 p-8 sm:p-10 backdrop-blur-2xl shadow-sm">
        <a href={`${base}/projects`} class="text-base font-bold text-slate-700 hover:text-emerald-700 transition-colors">
          ← Back to All Case Studies
        </a>
        <a
          href={`${base}/contact`}
          class="inline-flex items-center rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-600 to-brand-500 px-6 py-3.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-glow hover:from-emerald-500 hover:to-brand-400 transition-all"
        >
          Discuss Your HR Architecture
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

